---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const ST = "server/src/iki_server/storage";
const REC = `${ST}/receipts.py`;
const CNT = `${ST}/reconciliations.py`;

const H = {
  short: "Checking material in, and counting what's there",
  how: "Request receipts, supplier deliveries, counts and stability pulls",
  example: "A reagent delivery, received into storage",
  rules: "Receipts, counts and pulls in full",
  ref: "Routes, code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "receipts", label: "Receiving a request's tubes" },
  { id: "deliveries", label: "Receiving a supplier's delivery" },
  { id: "counts", label: "Counting a container" },
  { id: "pulls", label: "Stability pulls" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A service receives a request's tubes on a receipt: each expected tube is a line, scanned or
      marked, and completing the receipt takes custody, puts each away and tells the requester of
      anything that didn't arrive as expected. A supplier delivery arrives through an action that
      creates lots straight into storage. A count compares what's scanned in a container's positions
      with what's recorded, and applies its resolutions as one change. Receipts and counts each carry
      a revision, so a person completes what they reviewed (<Adr
        n={[180, 190, 207]}
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <h3 id="receipts">Receiving a request's tubes</h3>
    <p>
      A request type's <code>receives</code> names the list it's received against and the service's
      lab roles that may receive it; in <code>iki/requests</code>, the tubes, by its coordinators. A
      receiver starts a receipt, which has a line for each tube the request expects that no completed
      receipt received; a request has one open receipt at a time (<Path p={REC} sym="def start(" />, <Path
        p={`${ST}/models.py`}
        sym='name="iki_storage_receipt_one_open"'
      />). Each line is scanned or
      ticked as matched, missing, damaged or rejected, and a code that isn't expected is an extra line.
      Every observation is an append-only event with its before and after (<Path
        p={`${ST}/observations.py`}
      />).
    </p>
    <p>
      Completing it needs who handed it over, such as a courier and its waybill, every line checked, a
      note on each damaged, rejected or extra line, and each matched or damaged tube either put away
      or kept in custody. Then it takes custody of what arrived, puts it away through a reviewed move
      plan, freezes the receipt, and tells the request's submitter and watchers of what didn't arrive
      as expected (<Path p={REC} sym="def complete(" />, <Path p={REC} sym="def _tell(" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="deliveries">Receiving a supplier's delivery</h3>
    <p>
      An action's <code>creates</code> effect with <code>receive_into</code> names the input container
      each new record goes into. The run makes the record, opens its amount and places it in the run's
      transaction, with the run as the move's operation; a delivery must create a fresh record (<Path
        p="server/src/iki_server/runs/results.py"
        sym="def _place_received("
      />). A project's stock is the balances of its lots, with physical stock and what's available for
      routine use shown apart, and an hourly check tells its stock managers once per low-stock episode
      (<Adr n="0190" />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/amounts/stock.py" />, <Path
        p="server/src/iki_server/amounts/stock_alerts.py"
      />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="counts">Counting a container</h3>
    <p>
      A count notes what's recorded in each of a container's positions as it starts. Each position
      scanned says what's there, or that it's empty, in any order or from a rack scanner's file. A
      record is then matched, missing, unexpected or in the wrong position, and each that isn't
      matched is resolved: moved to where it was found, taken out of storage, put where it was found,
      or left as recorded with a note. Completing it applies every resolution as one change, and is
      refused if anything moved into or out of the container since it started (<Path
        p={CNT}
        sym="def complete("
      />, <Path p={CNT} sym="storage.events_since(container, reconciliation.started_at)" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="pulls">Stability pulls</h3>
    <p>
      A stability pull is the scheduled use of one tube of one lot at a condition and time point.
      Its <code>draw_target</code> takes one draw from its assigned tube, following its assigned lot, while
      the pull is scheduled, by a coordinator, once the study revision is pinned and the tube is in
      storage, in exactly the planned volume (<Adr n="0193" />, <Path
        p={`server/src/iki_server/amounts/services.py`}
        sym="def _check_draw_target("
      />):
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/stability/types/pull.yaml" start="^draw_target:" />
    <p>How draws are checked in general is on <PageLink to="Draws and samples" />.</p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      A reagent order arrives. <code>iki/reagents</code>' <code>receive_delivery</code> action creates
      a stock lot for the delivery line, by mass, volume or count, and puts it in storage as it
      records it, at the chosen slot or the first free one:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/reagents/actions/receive_delivery.yaml" start="^effects:" />
    <p>
      A volume lot keeps its amount in millilitres, in the catalogue item's stock unit. Every stock
      lot is an <code>iki/lots.Lot</code>, so it starts quarantined, and until QA releases it only a QA
      sampling draw may take from it (the lot's guards are on <PageLink
        to="Draws and samples"
        hash="checks"
      />). A repeated delivery line can't post a second receipt, and an occupied position, a stale
      order or a duplicate leaves the order and stock as they were (<Adr n="0190" />, <Path
        p="plugins/reagents/types/stock_lot.yaml"
      />, <Path p="plugins/reagents/types/volume_stock_lot.yaml" />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Receipts" open>
        <p>
          Describing, previewing, completing or cancelling a receipt names the revision it was
          reviewed at, and changing a line's outcome names the line's. A stale one is refused with 409, listing the lines that changed since and their revisions, so the receiver
          reviews them again (<Path p={REC} sym="class LinesChanged(" />). A put-away position the
          server allocated must be one the receiver saw in the preview; otherwise completing answers
          409 <code>moves_plan_changed</code> with the positions it would use now.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Counts">
        <p>
          A count carries a revision too, and editing it advances it (<Path p={CNT} sym="def _advance_plan(" />).
          A count never passes an empty position to the move planner, which would allocate a free slot
          of its own: a record is moved or put only at the position it was scanned in. A position not
          scanned is refused at completion unless the person marks the rest missing (<Adr
            n={[180, 207]}
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Stability pulls">
        <p>
          A pull draws once: a second draw for it is refused, and so is one from another tube or lot, or
          of another volume (<Adr n="0193" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <Routes tags={["storage"]} paths={/^\/api\/v1\/(receipts|reconciliations|entities\/\{ref\}\/receipts|storage\/(awaiting-put-away|containers\/\{ref\}\/reconciliations))/} />
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={REC} />: receiving a request's material</li>
        <li><Path p={CNT} />: counting a container</li>
        <li><Path p={`${ST}/observations.py`} />: the append-only observations of both</li>
        <li><Path p="plugins/reagents" />, <Path p="plugins/stability" />: deliveries and pulls</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0180" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0190" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0193" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0207" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
